# Mesh-accelerated slab-based dispersion Ewald (pppm/disp/slab) for a planar LJ
# liquid-vapor slab -- typically the fastest accurate long-range dispersion for
# planar interfaces.  Pairs with the matched lj/cut/dispswitch pair style; the
# smooth switched correction is folded into the mesh influence function, so one
# FFT pass yields the energy, force and full pressure tensor.

units           lj
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p p

read_data       data.lj_slab

# matched pair: r_cut = 2.5, switch width Delta = 0.5
pair_style      lj/cut/dispswitch 2.5 0.5
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0

kspace_style    pppm/disp/slab 1.0e-4

variable        lz equal lz
variable        gamma equal 0.5*v_lz*(pzz-0.5*(pxx+pyy))
thermo_style    custom step temp pe etotal press pxx pyy pzz v_gamma
thermo          50

velocity        all create 0.85 4928 mom yes
fix             1 all nve
timestep        0.004
run             500
